{
    "article_summary": "The article describes a dual phosphine and photoredox catalytic system for the anti-Markovnikov hydroamination of unactivated olefins with primary sulfonamides. The reaction proceeds via a phosphoranyl radical intermediate that undergoes alpha-scission to generate sulfonamidyl radicals, a pathway that is catalytic in phosphine (PCy3) and avoids the stoichiometric phosphine oxide waste typical of beta-scission processes.",
